    "last_assistant_text": "The PoC triggered the vulnerability successfully. The ASAN output confirms:\n\n- **Heap-use-after-free READ of size 2** at `HashMgr::add_word` (hashmgr.cxx:389) — the `TESTAFF(dp->astr, ONLYUPCASEFLAG, dp->alen)` call reads 2 bytes from freed heap memory\n- **Freed at** `HashMgr::add_word` (hashmgr.cxx:390) — the `delete[] dp->astr` that frees the shared alias table entry\n- **Allocated at** `HashMgr::decode_flags` → `HashMgr::parse_aliasf` — the original alias table allocation\n\nThe root cause: when a flag alias in FLAG UTF-8 mode contains character U+FFE7 (which maps to `ONLYUPCASEFLAG = 65511`), the `add_word` function mistakenly treats an aliased flag pointer as a privately-owned allocation and frees it with `delete[]`. Subsequent accesses to the same alias entry read freed heap memory.",
